<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"> <P STYLE=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman; " ALIGN="left">&#147;<B><I><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">As-Converted</FONT> Exchange Ratio</I></B>&#148; means the ratio
(rounded down to ten decimal places) equal to the quotient obtained by dividing (1)&nbsp;the Company Merger Shares by (2)&nbsp;the Company Outstanding Shares. </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
<P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
<TABLE STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%">
